  "titleEn": "Shopping",
  "grammarTip": "When you talk about quantities and prices, the noun that follows goes into the genitive case. After the numbers 2, 3 and 4 use the genitive singular: dva kilograma, tri eura; from 5 upward, and after quantity words like kilogram and litar, use the genitive plural: pet eura, kilogram krompira (a kilo of potatoes), litar mlijeka (a liter of milk). To ask a price, use 'Koliko košta...?' (How much does... cost?) — the thing being priced itself stays in the nominative: Koliko košta hljeb?",
